DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The oobbjjccooppyy utility copies the content of the binary object named by ar‐
     gument _i_n_f_i_l_e to that named by argument _o_u_t_f_i_l_e, transforming it accord‐
     ing to the command line options specified.  If argument _o_u_t_f_i_l_e is not
     specified, oobbjjccooppyy will create a temporary file and will subsequently re‐
     name it as _i_n_f_i_l_e.

     The oobbjjccooppyy utility supports the following options:

     --II _o_b_j_f_o_r_m_a_t | --ss _o_b_j_f_o_r_m_a_t | ----iinnppuutt--ttaarrggeett==_o_b_j_f_o_r_m_a_t
             Specify that the input file named by the argument _i_n_f_i_l_e is in
             the object format specified by the argument _o_b_j_f_o_r_m_a_t.

     --KK _s_y_m_b_o_l_n_a_m_e | ----kkeeeepp--ssyymmbbooll==_s_y_m_b_o_l_n_a_m_e
             Copy the symbol named by argument _s_y_m_b_o_l_n_a_m_e to the output.

     --LL _s_y_m_b_o_l_n_a_m_e | ----llooccaalliizzee--ssyymmbbooll==_s_y_m_b_o_l_n_a_m_e
             Make the symbol named by argument _s_y_m_b_o_l_n_a_m_e local to the output
             file.

     --NN _s_y_m_b_o_l | ----ssttrriipp--ssyymmbbooll==_s_y_m_b_o_l_n_a_m_e
             Do not copy the symbol named by argument _s_y_m_b_o_l_n_a_m_e to the out‐
             put.

     --OO _o_b_j_f_o_r_m_a_t | ----oouuttppuutt--ttaarrggeett==_o_b_j_f_o_r_m_a_t
             Write the output file using the object format specified in argu‐
             ment _o_b_j_f_o_r_m_a_t.  The argument _o_b_j_f_o_r_m_a_t should be one of the tar‐
             get names recognized by elftc_bfd_find_target(3).

     --RR _s_e_c_t_i_o_n_n_a_m_e | ----rreemmoovvee--sseeccttiioonn==_s_e_c_t_i_o_n_n_a_m_e
             Remove any section with name _s_e_c_t_i_o_n_n_a_m_e from the output file.

     --SS | ----ssttrriipp--aallll
             Do not copy symbol and relocation information to the target file.

     --VV | ----vveerrssiioonn
             Print a version identifier and exit.

     --WW _s_y_m_b_o_l_n_a_m_e | ----wweeaakkeenn--ssyymmbbooll==_s_y_m_b_o_l_n_a_m_e
             Mark the symbol named by argument _s_y_m_b_o_l_n_a_m_e as weak in the out‐
             put.

     --XX | ----ddiissccaarrdd--llooccaallss
             Do not copy compiler generated local symbols to the output.

     --dd | --gg | ----ssttrriipp--ddeebbuugg
             Do not copy debugging information to the target file.

     --hh | ----hheellpp
             Display a help message and exit.

     --jj _s_e_c_t_i_o_n_n_a_m_e | ----oonnllyy--sseeccttiioonn==_s_e_c_t_i_o_n_n_a_m_e
             Copy only the section named by argument _s_e_c_t_i_o_n_n_a_m_e to the out‐
             put.

     --pp | ----pprreesseerrvvee--ddaatteess
             Set the access and modification times of the output file to the
             same as those of the input.

     --ww | ----wwiillddccaarrdd
             Use shell-style patterns to name symbols.  The following meta-
             characters are recognized in patterns:
             !     If this is the first character of the pattern, invert the
                   sense of the pattern match.
             *     Matches any string of characters in a symbol name.
             ?     Matches zero or one character in a symbol name.
             [     Mark the start of a character class.
             \     Remove the special meaning of the next character in the
                   pattern.
             ]     Mark the end of a character class.

     --xx | ----ddiissccaarrdd--aallll
             Do not copy non-global symbols to the output.

     ----aadddd--ggnnuu--ddeebbuugglliinnkk=_f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e
             Create a .gnu_debuglink section in the output file that refer‐
             ences the debug data in _f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e.

     ----aadddd--sseeccttiioonn _s_e_c_t_i_o_n_n_a_m_e=_f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e
             Add a new section to the output file with name _s_e_c_t_i_o_n_n_a_m_e.  The
             contents of the section are taken from the file named by argument
             _f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e.  The size of the section will be the number of bytes in
             file _f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e.

     ----aaddjjuusstt--sseeccttiioonn--vvmmaa _s_e_c_t_i_o_n{+|-|=}_v_a_l | ----cchhaannggee--sseeccttiioonn--aaddddrreessss
             _s_e_c_t_i_o_n{+|-|=}_v_a_l
             Depending on the operator specified, increase, decrease or set
             both the virtual memory address and the load memory address of
             the section named by the argument _s_e_c_t_i_o_n.  The argument _v_a_l
             specifies the desired increment, decrement or new value for the
             address.

     ----aaddjjuusstt--ssttaarrtt=_i_n_c_r_e_m_e_n_t | ----cchhaannggee--ssttaarrtt=_i_n_c_r_e_m_e_n_t
             Increase the entry point address of the output ELF object by the
             value specified in the argument _i_n_c_r_e_m_e_n_t.

     ----aaddjjuusstt--vvmmaa=_i_n_c_r_e_m_e_n_t | ----cchhaannggee--aaddddrreesssseess=_i_n_c_r_e_m_e_n_t
             Increase the virtual memory address and the load memory address
             of all sections by the value specified by the argument _i_n_c_r_e_m_e_n_t.

     ----aaddjjuusstt--wwaarrnniinnggss | ----cchhaannggee--wwaarrnniinnggss
             Issue a warning if the section specified by the options
             ----cchhaannggee--sseeccttiioonn--aaddddrreessss, ----cchhaannggee--sseeccttiioonn--llmmaa or
             ----cchhaannggee--sseeccttiioonn--vvmmaa does not exist in the input object.  This is
             the default.

     ----cchhaannggee--sseeccttiioonn--llmmaa _s_e_c_t_i_o_n{+|-|=}_v_a_l
             Change or set the load memory address of the section named by the
             argument _s_e_c_t_i_o_n.  Depending on the operator specified, the value
             in argument _v_a_l will be used as an increment, a decrement or as
             the new value of the load memory address.

     ----cchhaannggee--sseeccttiioonn--vvmmaa _s_e_c_t_i_o_n{+|-|=}_v_a_l
             Change or set the virtual memory address of the section named by
             the argument _s_e_c_t_i_o_n.  Depending on the operator specified, the
             value in argument _v_a_l will be used as an increment, a decrement
             or as the new value of the virtual memory address.

     ----eexxttrraacctt--ddwwoo
